From 9e536fd04e06cebed77bff82625e0c7f8a85af8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 03:21:36 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(desktop): remote-update boot wait cap is hard;
 refusal phrase is one shared constant

Follow-up to the non-blocking nits of review 5889912621 on PR #2112.

1. Hard 30 min cap. At the cap use-gateway-boot reset the RemoteUpdateWait before the
   bounded-retry branch, so a bounded retry (stage 'dialing' or a retryable:true boot
   snapshot) that met the same refusal opened a fresh 30 min wait, and the overlay could be
   postponed indefinitely. The wait now resets only on a successful boot, a non-update
   failure, or a connection switch. New test: past the cap with a retryable snapshot, the
   bounded branch retries its 5 attempts and the overlay shows within cap + 5 s poll + 44 s
   bounded budget (fails on 8af368b973: no overlay; passes here).
2. Drop the test-only RemoteUpdateWait.waiting getter; the unit test asserts the spent-cap
   behaviour through next() instead.
3. electron/remote-update-refusal.ts exports REMOTE_UPDATE_PAUSED_PHRASE. The three
   producers (remote-lifecycle, windows-remote-lifecycle, remote-update-pause) build their
   refusal from it and the renderer matcher imports it, replacing the test that regex-read
   electron/*.ts source.

Tests: vitest remote-update-wait.test.ts + use-gateway-boot-remote-update.test.tsx (7 pass),
electron remote-update-pause/remote-dial-backoff/remote-lifecycle* (176 pass); tsc (renderer,
electron) clean for desktop files; eslint clean.
